-- The glider, acted out (c2): one statement, repeated, is the flipbook — one barrier per generation. Twin of c2-life-glider.bqn.
-- 8x8 lattice, moore 8-stencil; population queries bracket the run (a glider carries 5 cells forever).
-- Four statements, four generations: the post-state is the seed translated one cell down-right. Installed with the arrow instead (§11), the same line runs one generation per tick — the flora act it out on the world clock and the statement log stays empty.
